{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Recipes","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/SwiftUIAndUIKitEquivalents"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":" class that owns a screen’s "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},{"type":"text","text":" and knows how to run an async load. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":" switches on that state, rendering your content only for the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" case and a placeholder otherwise."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import SwiftUI","import ScreenStates","","struct ArticlesScreen: View {","    @State private var store = ScreenStateStore<[Article]>()","","    var body: some View {","        ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: reload) { articles in","            List(articles) { article in","                Text(article.title)","            }","        }","        .task { await reload() }","    }","","    private func reload() async {","        await store.loadCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" sets "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":", runs the closure, and maps the outcome to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"type":"text","text":" (when the result is an empty collection), or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":" shows the default Loading spinner, Empty placeholder, or Error view — with a working Retry button wired to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onRetry"},{"text":" — automatically.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you’d rather not wrap the whole call site in an initializer, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".screenState(_:onRetry:content:)"},{"text":" is the same thing as a view modifier:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["EmptyView()","    .screenState(store.state, onRetry: reload) { articles in","        List(articles) { article in Text(article.title) }","    }"]},{"text":"Customizing the placeholders","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Customizing-the-placeholders"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"empty"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loading"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"error"},{"type":"text","text":" view builders to fully replace the defaults:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateView(store.state) { articles in","    ArticleList(articles)","} empty: {","    ContentUnavailableView(\"No Articles Yet\", systemImage: \"newspaper\")","} loading: {","    ProgressView(\"Loading articles…\")","} error: { error in","    MyErrorBanner(error: error, retry: reload)","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A fully custom placeholder like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MyErrorBanner"},{"type":"text","text":" can still announce transitions to VoiceOver with the same wording the default placeholders use, via "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".onAppear {","    if let announcement = state.accessibilityAnnouncement {","        AccessibilityNotification.Announcement(announcement).post()","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" — your own content is what VoiceOver should read at that point — and, for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".empty"},{"text":", it’s the default “Nothing Here” text; announce your own custom title directly instead if your placeholder shows one, so VoiceOver matches what’s on screen.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Refreshing without losing data","anchor":"Refreshing-without-losing-data","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" always shows "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"text":" first, which is right for the initial fetch but wrong for pull-to-refresh — the list shouldn’t disappear behind a spinner while it’s being refetched. Use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection(_:)"},{"text":" instead: it keeps the current ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"text":" on screen while the operation runs, and leaves it there if the operation fails instead of switching to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["List(articles) { article in","    Text(article.title)","}",".refreshable {","    await store.refreshCollection { try await api.fetchArticles() }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the duration; a failure is reported via "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"store.refreshError"},{"type":"text","text":" rather than by discarding "},{"code":"state","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so the list stays visible and you can surface the error separately (a toast, for example)."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Retrying on failure","level":2,"anchor":"Retrying-on-failure"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a flaky call worth retrying automatically before showing an error, use "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadWithRetry(maxAttempts:backoff:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["await store.loadWithRetry(maxAttempts: 3) {","    try await api.fetchArticles()","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" stays "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".loading"},{"type":"text","text":" across every attempt; only the final failure, once "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxAttempts"},{"type":"text","text":" is exhausted, switches it to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".error"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"backoff"},{"type":"text","text":" is called with the attempt number that just failed and returns how long to wait before the next try, defaulting to doubling from one second."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Overlapping-calls-are-safe","type":"heading","text":"Overlapping calls are safe"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Nothing extra is needed to handle a screen firing off a second ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadWithRetry(_:)"},{"text":" call before an earlier one has finished — a fast double-tap on Retry, or a new query arriving before the previous one resolved. ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" only ever applies the most recently started call’s result; a slower, now-stale response landing late is dropped instead of overwriting state a newer call already produced.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Cancelling-an-in-flight-call","type":"heading","text":"Cancelling an in-flight call"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Call ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/cancel()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" to stop whatever call is currently running, without waiting for it to resolve — useful from ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDisappear"},{"text":", or right before firing off a newer query:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swif